//@version=6
// ==============================================================================================
//                        T R E N D   B R E A K O U T   E N T R I E S
// ==============================================================================================
//
//  Indicator Name : Trend Breakout Entries
//  Author         : Michael_Fx_Trader
//  Version        : v6.0 - July 2026
//  Pine Version   : Pine Script v6
//  Script Type    : Overlay indicator (plots on the price chart)
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  A U T H O R   V E R I F I C A T I O N   D E C L A R A T I O N
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  I am Michael_Fx_Trader, the publisher and sole original author of this exact implementation of
//  "Trend Breakout Entries." I designed the architecture of this tool, wrote every line of the
//  Pine Script v6 code contained in this file, tested it across multiple asset classes and
//  timeframes, and I take full and sole ownership and responsibility for it.
//
//  Specifically, I independently designed and coded: the volatility-adaptive pivot detection that
//  locates the swing highs and swing lows; the two-point trendline construction that connects the
//  two most recent qualifying highs into a falling resistance line and the two most recent
//  qualifying lows into a rising support line; the live projection of each line forward to the
//  current bar; the breakout test that requires a decisive close beyond the projected line by an
//  ATR-scaled margin; the strength filter built from close distance, candle body, momentum and
//  relative volume that separates a genuine breakout from a marginal poke; the retest tracking that
//  marks the return to a broken line; the signal state machine and cooldown; the trade projection;
//  the dashboard; and the alert framework.
//
//  This declaration is made for this specific version of the script (v6.0, July 2026). Any future
//  modified version I publish will carry its own updated declaration in this same header.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  O R I G I N A L   I N D I C A T O R   S C R I P T   I M P L E M E N T A T I O N
//  V E R I F I C A T I O N   A N D   D E C L A R A T I O N
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  I verify and declare that this script is an original implementation authored from scratch by
//  Michael_Fx_Trader. No portion of this code was copied, ported, decompiled, translated,
//  reverse-engineered or adapted from any other author's closed-source, invite-only, protected or
//  open-source script. No third-party library and no republished open-source script forms any part
//  of this work, and no other author's trendline logic or visual system was reproduced.
//
//  I acknowledge openly that the underlying trading concepts are public and widely taught. Trend
//  lines drawn across swing highs and swing lows, the reading of a decisive close beyond such a
//  line as a breakout, and the tendency of a broken line to be retested from the other side, are
//  all common knowledge across the trading community and belong to no single author.
//
//  My original contribution, and what this declaration covers, is the specific code
//  implementation: my own adaptive pivot detection, my own trendline construction and projection,
//  my own ATR-scaled breakout test, my own multi-factor strength filter, my own retest tracking, my
//  own signal state machine, my own trade projection, and my own presentation layer. Conceptual
//  overlap with other trendline breakout tools is therefore unavoidable and expected, but there is
//  no source-code overlap of any kind with any other author's work.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  W H A T   T H I S   I N D I C A T O R   D O E S
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Trend Breakout Entries draws the two trendlines that matter, watches for a decisive break of
//  either, and signals only when that break is strong rather than marginal.
//
//  1) SWING DETECTION
//     Swing highs and swing lows are located by a pivot routine whose confirmation window widens
//     and narrows with volatility, so the swings stay meaningful whether the market is fast or slow.
//
//  2) TWO TRENDLINES
//     The two most recent qualifying swing highs are connected into an upper line, the resistance
//     that a rally must clear. The two most recent qualifying swing lows are connected into a lower
//     line, the support that a decline must break. Each line is projected forward to the current
//     bar so its live value is always known.
//
//  3) BREAKOUT DETECTION
//     A buy is considered when price closes above the upper line by more than an ATR-scaled margin.
//     A sell is considered when price closes below the lower line by the same kind of margin. The
//     margin is what separates a real break from a wick that grazed the line and closed back inside.
//
//  4) STRENGTH FILTER
//     A close beyond the line is necessary but not sufficient. The break is scored on how far beyond
//     the line price closed, how solid the breakout candle's body was, whether momentum agreed, and
//     whether volume was elevated. Only a break that clears the strength threshold is signalled, so
//     a strong breakout is marked and a limp one is ignored.
//
//  5) RETEST AWARENESS
//     After a line breaks, price often returns to it before continuing. That retest is tracked and
//     marked, because the retest of a broken line is frequently a higher-quality entry than the
//     break itself.
//
//  6) TRADE PROJECTION
//     On a signal, entry, stop and targets are projected. The stop sits back beyond the broken line
//     by an ATR margin; the targets are set at reward multiples of that risk.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  U N I V E R S A L   M A R K E T   A N D   T I M E F R A M E   C O M P A T I B I L I T Y
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Every distance in this tool is an ATR multiple or a ratio, so no pip value, point distance or
//  price constant appears anywhere. The same settings behave correctly on Forex, gold and other
//  metals, indices, crypto, futures and equities, from seconds charts to monthly. The volume term
//  in the strength filter uses a Universal Activity source, real volume where the feed publishes
//  it and a synthetic estimate otherwise, so the filter never breaks on volume-less feeds. The
//  breakout logic itself needs no volume at all.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  L I V E   B E H A V I O U R   A N D   R E P A I N T I N G   S T A T E M E N T
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  A swing is confirmed only after the required bars have formed to its right, which is inherent to
//  every pivot-based tool. Once confirmed, a swing anchor is fixed; the trendline drawn from two
//  fixed anchors does not move, and only re-draws when a newer qualifying swing replaces an anchor.
//  Breakout and retest signals are confirmed on bar close and never repaint: a printed signal never
//  disappears from history.
//
//  No request.security call is used, so there is no higher-timeframe lookahead of any kind.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  H O N E S T   N O T E
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  A two-point trendline is, by definition, drawn from two swings, and a swing is only known after
//  it has been confirmed by the bars to its right. The line is therefore always based on completed
//  structure, and the break of it is judged on a closed bar. Not every breakout continues; some
//  fail and reverse, which is why the strength filter and the stop both exist. The strength score
//  is a filter, not a probability or a guarantee.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  D I S C L A I M E R
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  This tool is for educational and informational purposes only. It does not constitute financial
//  advice. Trading involves risk; past patterns do not guarantee future results. Use proper risk
//  management and consult a licensed financial advisor before trading real capital.
// ==============================================================================================

indicator("Trend Breakout Entries", "Trend Breakout", overlay = true, max_lines_count = 500, max_labels_count = 500, max_bars_back = 1000)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  I N P U T S
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
gSw = "=====  SWING DETECTION  ====="
minSwing = input.int(5,  "Minimum Swing Bars", minval = 2, maxval = 30, group = gSw, tooltip = "Confirmation bars on each side of a pivot when volatility is high.")
maxSwing = input.int(15, "Maximum Swing Bars", minval = 3, maxval = 60, group = gSw, tooltip = "Confirmation bars when volatility is low.")
atrLen   = input.int(14, "ATR Length", minval = 2, maxval = 200, group = gSw)
volFast  = input.int(10, "Volatility Fast ATR", minval = 2, maxval = 100, group = gSw)
volSlow  = input.int(50, "Volatility Slow ATR", minval = 5, maxval = 300, group = gSw)
swMemory = input.int(6, "Swing Points Remembered (each side)", minval = 2, maxval = 12, group = gSw, tooltip = "How many recent swing highs and swing lows are kept. Trendlines are drawn between these, so more points means more lines.")
maxActive= input.int(6, "Max Active Trendlines (each side)", minval = 1, maxval = 12, group = gSw, tooltip = "How many resistance and support trendlines can be live and monitored for a breakout at once.")

gBrk = "=====  BREAKOUT  ====="
brkMargin = input.float(0.15, "Breakout Margin (x ATR)", minval = 0.0, maxval = 3, step = 0.05, group = gBrk, tooltip = "How far beyond the trendline price must close to count as a break. This is what filters out wicks that closed back inside.")
minStr    = input.float(2.5, "Minimum Strength (0-4)", minval = 1, maxval = 4, step = 0.5, group = gBrk, tooltip = "How many of the four strength factors must agree for the breakout to signal.")
useMom    = input.bool(true, "Require Momentum Agreement", group = gBrk)
rsiLen    = input.int(14, "RSI Length", minval = 2, maxval = 100, group = gBrk)
useVol    = input.bool(true, "Require Elevated Volume", group = gBrk)
cooldown  = input.int(8, "Bars Between Signals", minval = 0, maxval = 100, group = gBrk)

gRt = "=====  RETEST  ====="
showRetest = input.bool(true, "Mark Line Retests", group = gRt, tooltip = "After a line breaks, marks price returning to it, which is often a higher-quality entry than the break.")
retestATR  = input.float(0.25, "Retest Proximity (x ATR)", minval = 0.05, maxval = 3, step = 0.05, group = gRt)
retestBars = input.int(30, "Retest Valid For (bars)", minval = 3, maxval = 200, group = gRt)

gLn = "=====  TRENDLINES  ====="
showLines = input.bool(true, "Show Trendlines", group = gLn)
extendBars= input.int(15, "Project Forward (bars)", minval = 0, maxval = 200, group = gLn)
lineW     = input.int(2, "Line Width", minval = 1, maxval = 5, group = gLn)
keepBroken= input.bool(true, "Dim Broken Lines", group = gLn, tooltip = "Keeps a broken line drawn but dimmed so its retest can still be seen.")

gTr = "=====  TRADE PROJECTION  ====="
showTrade = input.bool(true, "Show Entry / Stop / Target Lines", group = gTr)
stopATR   = input.float(0.6, "Stop Beyond Line (x ATR)", minval = 0.1, maxval = 5, step = 0.1, group = gTr)
tp1RR     = input.float(1.0, "Target 1 (R multiple)", minval = 0.5, maxval = 10, step = 0.5, group = gTr)
tp2RR     = input.float(2.0, "Target 2 (R multiple)", minval = 0.5, maxval = 10, step = 0.5, group = gTr)
tp3RR     = input.float(3.0, "Target 3 (R multiple)", minval = 0.5, maxval = 10, step = 0.5, group = gTr)
showTradeLbl = input.bool(false, "Show Trade Level Labels", group = gTr, tooltip = "OFF draws clean lines only. ON prints ENTRY, STOP and TARGET text.")
tradeExt  = input.int(30, "Trade Line Extend (bars)", minval = 5, maxval = 200, group = gTr)

gDash = "=====  DASHBOARD  ====="
showDash = input.bool(true, "Show Dashboard", group = gDash)
dashPos  = input.string("Top Right", "Position", options = ["Top Right", "Middle Right", "Bottom Right", "Top Left", "Bottom Left"], group = gDash)

gAct = "=====  ACTIVITY SOURCE  (strength filter)  ====="
actMode = input.string("Auto", "Volume Source", options = ["Auto", "Chart Volume Only", "Synthetic Estimate"], group = gAct)

gSty = "=====  STYLE  ====="
colUp   = input.color(#26a69a, "Support Line / Buy", group = gSty, inline = "a")
colDn   = input.color(#ef5350, "Resistance Line / Sell", group = gSty, inline = "a")
colRt   = input.color(#f0b90b, "Retest", group = gSty)
colDashB= input.color(#0b1020, "Dashboard Background", group = gSty)
colDashT= input.color(#d1d4dc, "Dashboard Text", group = gSty)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  U N I V E R S A L   A C T I V I T Y   ( strength filter only )
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
float rawVol  = nz(volume)
bool  hasReal = ta.cum(rawVol) > 0 and not na(volume)
float trueR   = ta.tr(true)
float baseA   = ta.atr(20)
float eff     = trueR > 0 ? math.abs(close - open) / trueR : 0.0
float synth   = baseA > 0 ? math.max(0.0, (trueR / baseA) * (0.55 + 0.45 * eff) * 1000.0) : 0.0
float actVol  = actMode == "Chart Volume Only" ? rawVol : actMode == "Synthetic Estimate" ? synth : (hasReal ? rawVol : synth)
float actAvg  = ta.sma(actVol, 20)

float atr = ta.atr(atrLen)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  A D A P T I V E   S W I N G   W I N D O W
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
float aFast   = ta.atr(volFast)
float aSlow   = ta.atr(volSlow)
float volRat  = aSlow > 0 ? aFast / aSlow : 1.0
float volRank = nz(ta.percentrank(volRat, 100), 50.0)
int   hiSw    = math.max(minSwing, maxSwing)
int   swLen   = math.max(minSwing, math.min(hiSw, int(math.round(hiSw - (hiSw - minSwing) * volRank / 100.0))))

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  S W I N G   S T O R E
//  We remember the last swMemory confirmed swing highs and swing lows, each with its bar index.
//  Trendlines are then built between pairs of these, so lines appear all across the chart on both
//  sides rather than only from the single most recent pair.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
float ph = ta.pivothigh(high, swLen, swLen)
float pl = ta.pivotlow(low,  swLen, swLen)

var array<float> hiP = array.new<float>()   // swing high prices, newest at end
var array<int>   hiX = array.new<int>()      // their bar indices
var array<int>   hiT = array.new<int>()      // their bar times
var array<float> loP = array.new<float>()
var array<int>   loX = array.new<int>()
var array<int>   loT = array.new<int>()

if not na(ph)
    hiP.push(ph)
    hiX.push(bar_index - swLen)
    hiT.push(int(time[swLen]))
    if hiP.size() > swMemory
        hiP.shift()
        hiX.shift()
        hiT.shift()
if not na(pl)
    loP.push(pl)
    loX.push(bar_index - swLen)
    loT.push(int(time[swLen]))
    if loP.size() > swMemory
        loP.shift()
        loX.shift()
        loT.shift()

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  T R E N D L I N E   T Y P E
//  isRes = true  -> resistance line built from two swing highs (break UP = buy)
//  isRes = false -> support line built from two swing lows  (break DOWN = sell)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
type TL
    float p1
    int   x1
    int   t1
    float p2
    int   x2
    int   t2
    float slope
    bool  isRes
    bool  broken
    int   brkBar
    int   bornBar
    line  ln

var array<TL> tls = array.new<TL>()

method valueAt(TL t, int bx) =>
    t.p2 + t.slope * (bx - t.x2)

method wipe(TL t) =>
    line.delete(t.ln)

trimSide(bool res) =>
    int count = 0
    if tls.size() > 0
        for m = tls.size() - 1 to 0
            TL t = tls.get(m)
            if t.isRes == res and not t.broken
                count += 1
                if count > maxActive
                    t.wipe()
                    tls.remove(m)

// build a fresh set of candidate trendlines from the current swing store, on each new pivot
buildLines() =>
    // resistance lines: connect pairs of highs where the line does not cut through price between them
    int nH = hiP.size()
    if nH >= 2
        for i = nH - 1 to 1
            for j = i - 1 to math.max(0, i - 3)
                int   x1 = hiX.get(j)
                float y1 = hiP.get(j)
                int   x2 = hiX.get(i)
                float y2 = hiP.get(i)
                if x2 != x1
                    float sl = (y2 - y1) / (x2 - x1)
                    bool valid = true
                    if tls.size() > 0
                        for m = 0 to tls.size() - 1
                            TL e = tls.get(m)
                            if e.isRes and e.x2 == x2 and e.x1 == x1
                                valid := false
                    if valid
                        TL t = TL.new()
                        t.p1 := y1
                        t.x1 := x1
                        t.t1 := hiT.get(j)
                        t.p2 := y2
                        t.x2 := x2
                        t.t2 := hiT.get(i)
                        t.slope := sl
                        t.isRes := true
                        t.broken := false
                        t.brkBar := na
                        t.bornBar := bar_index
                        tls.push(t)
    int nL = loP.size()
    if nL >= 2
        for i = nL - 1 to 1
            for j = i - 1 to math.max(0, i - 3)
                int   x1 = loX.get(j)
                float y1 = loP.get(j)
                int   x2 = loX.get(i)
                float y2 = loP.get(i)
                if x2 != x1
                    float sl = (y2 - y1) / (x2 - x1)
                    bool valid = true
                    if tls.size() > 0
                        for m = 0 to tls.size() - 1
                            TL e = tls.get(m)
                            if not e.isRes and e.x2 == x2 and e.x1 == x1
                                valid := false
                    if valid
                        TL t = TL.new()
                        t.p1 := y1
                        t.x1 := x1
                        t.t1 := loT.get(j)
                        t.p2 := y2
                        t.x2 := x2
                        t.t2 := loT.get(i)
                        t.slope := sl
                        t.isRes := false
                        t.broken := false
                        t.brkBar := na
                        t.bornBar := bar_index
                        tls.push(t)

    // cap the number of active (unbroken) lines per side, dropping the oldest
    trimSide(true)
    trimSide(false)


if barstate.isconfirmed and (not na(ph) or not na(pl))
    buildLines()

// retire broken lines that are older than the retest window, and hard-cap total lines
if barstate.isconfirmed and tls.size() > 0
    for m = tls.size() - 1 to 0
        TL t = tls.get(m)
        if t.broken and not na(t.brkBar) and (bar_index - t.brkBar) > retestBars
            t.wipe()
            tls.remove(m)
    while tls.size() > (maxActive * 4)
        TL dropped = tls.shift()
        dropped.wipe()

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  S T R E N G T H   F I L T E R   ( shared, evaluated per candidate break )
//  Four dimensionless factors: distance of the close beyond the line, breakout candle body,
//  momentum agreement, and relative volume.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
float rsi = ta.rsi(close, rsiLen)
float rng = high - low
float body = math.abs(close - open)
float bodyFrac = rng > 0 ? body / rng : 0.0
float rvol = actAvg > 0 ? actVol / actAvg : 1.0

strengthUp(float line) =>
    float dist = atr > 0 and not na(line) ? math.min((close - line) / atr, 1.0) : 0.0
    float f1 = math.max(0.0, math.min(1.0, dist / math.max(brkMargin, 0.05)))
    float f2 = bodyFrac
    float f3 = (not useMom or (rsi > 50 and rsi > rsi[1])) ? 1.0 : 0.0
    float f4 = (not useVol or rvol >= 1.2) ? 1.0 : 0.0
    f1 + f2 + f3 + f4

strengthDn(float line) =>
    float dist = atr > 0 and not na(line) ? math.min((line - close) / atr, 1.0) : 0.0
    float f1 = math.max(0.0, math.min(1.0, dist / math.max(brkMargin, 0.05)))
    float f2 = bodyFrac
    float f3 = (not useMom or (rsi < 50 and rsi < rsi[1])) ? 1.0 : 0.0
    float f4 = (not useVol or rvol >= 1.2) ? 1.0 : 0.0
    f1 + f2 + f3 + f4

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  B R E A K O U T   S C A N   A C R O S S   A L L   L I V E   L I N E S
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
var int lastSig = -100000
float marginPx = atr * brkMargin
bool gap = (bar_index - lastSig) > cooldown

bool  buySig  = false
bool  sellSig = false
float upScore = 0.0
float dnScore = 0.0
float brokenLineLvl = na

bool  buyRetest  = false
bool  sellRetest = false

if barstate.isconfirmed and tls.size() > 0
    for m = tls.size() - 1 to 0
        TL t = tls.get(m)
        float lv = t.valueAt(bar_index)
        if not na(lv)
            if not t.broken
                if t.isRes and close > lv + marginPx
                    float sc = strengthUp(lv)
                    if sc >= minStr and gap and not buySig
                        buySig := true
                        upScore := sc
                        brokenLineLvl := lv
                        t.broken := true
                        t.brkBar := bar_index
                else if not t.isRes and close < lv - marginPx
                    float sc = strengthDn(lv)
                    if sc >= minStr and gap and not sellSig
                        sellSig := true
                        dnScore := sc
                        brokenLineLvl := lv
                        t.broken := true
                        t.brkBar := bar_index
            else if showRetest and not na(t.brkBar) and (bar_index - t.brkBar) <= retestBars
                if t.isRes and math.abs(low - lv) <= atr * retestATR and close > lv
                    buyRetest := true
                else if not t.isRes and math.abs(high - lv) <= atr * retestATR and close < lv
                    sellRetest := true

// live "nearest line" values for the dashboard: closest unbroken resistance above / support below
float resNow = na
float supNow = na
if tls.size() > 0
    float bestUp = na
    float bestDn = na
    for m = 0 to tls.size() - 1
        TL t = tls.get(m)
        if not t.broken
            float lv = t.valueAt(bar_index)
            if not na(lv)
                if t.isRes and lv >= close and (na(bestUp) or lv < bestUp)
                    bestUp := lv
                if not t.isRes and lv <= close and (na(bestDn) or lv > bestDn)
                    bestDn := lv
    resNow := bestUp
    supNow := bestDn

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  T R A D E   P R O J E C T I O N
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
var int   posDir  = 0
var float entryPx = na
var float stopPx  = na
var float t1Px = na
var float t2Px = na
var float t3Px = na

if buySig or sellSig
    lastSig := bar_index
    posDir  := buySig ? 1 : -1
    entryPx := close
    if buySig
        stopPx := brokenLineLvl - atr * stopATR
        float risk = entryPx - stopPx
        t1Px := entryPx + risk * tp1RR
        t2Px := entryPx + risk * tp2RR
        t3Px := entryPx + risk * tp3RR
    else
        stopPx := brokenLineLvl + atr * stopATR
        float risk = stopPx - entryPx
        t1Px := entryPx - risk * tp1RR
        t2Px := entryPx - risk * tp2RR
        t3Px := entryPx - risk * tp3RR

float lastRisk = not na(entryPx) and not na(stopPx) ? math.abs(entryPx - stopPx) : na

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  D R A W I N G   -   A L L   T R E N D L I N E S
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
int barMs = nz(timeframe.in_seconds(timeframe.period), 60) * 1000
if barstate.islast and showLines and tls.size() > 0
    for m = 0 to tls.size() - 1
        TL t = tls.get(m)
        line.delete(t.ln)
        int rx = bar_index + extendBars
        float ry = t.valueAt(rx)
        int   rt = time + barMs * extendBars                 // project forward in time
        color bc = t.isRes ? colDn : colUp
        color cc = t.broken ? (keepBroken ? color.new(bc, 68) : color.new(bc, 100)) : color.new(bc, 12)
        if not na(ry) and not na(t.t2)
            // draw from the newer anchor (t2) to the projected right edge, anchored in TIME so old
            // anchors far from the current bar still render without a bar-index range error
            t.ln := line.new(t.t2, t.p2, rt, ry, xloc = xloc.bar_time, color = cc, width = lineW, style = t.broken ? line.style_dashed : line.style_solid)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  D R A W I N G   -   S I G N A L S
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
plotshape(buySig,     "Buy Breakout",   shape.labelup,   location.belowbar, color = colUp, textcolor = color.white, text = "BUY",  size = size.small)
plotshape(sellSig,    "Sell Breakout",  shape.labeldown, location.abovebar, color = colDn, textcolor = color.white, text = "SELL", size = size.small)
plotshape(buyRetest and not buySig,  "Buy Retest",  shape.triangleup,   location.belowbar, color = colRt, size = size.tiny)
plotshape(sellRetest and not sellSig, "Sell Retest", shape.triangledown, location.abovebar, color = colRt, size = size.tiny)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  D R A W I N G   -   T R A D E   L E V E L S
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
var line  enL = na
var line  slL = na
var line  t1L = na
var line  t2L = na
var line  t3L = na
var label enLb = na
var label slLb = na
var label t1Lb = na
var label t2Lb = na
var label t3Lb = na

if showTrade and (buySig or sellSig)
    line.delete(enL)
    line.delete(slL)
    line.delete(t1L)
    line.delete(t2L)
    line.delete(t3L)
    label.delete(enLb)
    label.delete(slLb)
    label.delete(t1Lb)
    label.delete(t2Lb)
    label.delete(t3Lb)

    color dir = posDir == 1 ? colUp : colDn
    int rx = bar_index + tradeExt

    enL := line.new(bar_index, entryPx, rx, entryPx, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = color.new(dir, 10), width = 2)
    slL := line.new(bar_index, stopPx,  rx, stopPx,  xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = color.new(colDn, 20), style = line.style_dashed)
    t1L := line.new(bar_index, t1Px, rx, t1Px, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = color.new(colUp, 30), style = line.style_dotted)
    t2L := line.new(bar_index, t2Px, rx, t2Px, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = color.new(colUp, 25), style = line.style_dotted)
    t3L := line.new(bar_index, t3Px, rx, t3Px, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = color.new(colUp, 20), style = line.style_dotted)

    if showTradeLbl
        enLb := label.new(rx, entryPx, "ENTRY " + str.tostring(entryPx, format.mintick), xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(dir, 20), textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)
        slLb := label.new(rx, stopPx,  "STOP "  + str.tostring(stopPx,  format.mintick), xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(colDn, 20), textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)
        t1Lb := label.new(rx, t1Px, "TP1 " + str.tostring(t1Px, format.mintick), xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(colUp, 25), textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)
        t2Lb := label.new(rx, t2Px, "TP2 " + str.tostring(t2Px, format.mintick), xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(colUp, 25), textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)
        t3Lb := label.new(rx, t3Px, "TP3 " + str.tostring(t3Px, format.mintick), xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(colUp, 25), textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  D A S H B O A R D
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
var table dash = na

dashPosition() =>
    dashPos == "Middle Right" ? position.middle_right : dashPos == "Bottom Right" ? position.bottom_right : dashPos == "Top Left" ? position.top_left : dashPos == "Bottom Left" ? position.bottom_left : position.top_right

if barstate.islast and showDash
    table.delete(dash)
    dash := table.new(dashPosition(), 2, 8, border_width = 1, border_color = color.new(colDashT, 85), frame_width = 1, frame_color = color.new(colDashT, 75))

    color bgH = color.new(colDashB, 0)
    color bgR = color.new(colDashB, 14)
    color dim = color.new(colDashT, 45)

    float distRes = not na(resNow) and atr > 0 ? (close - resNow) / atr : na
    float distSup = not na(supNow) and atr > 0 ? (close - supNow) / atr : na

    // count active (unbroken) lines each side for the dashboard
    int resCount = 0
    int supCount = 0
    if tls.size() > 0
        for m = 0 to tls.size() - 1
            TL t = tls.get(m)
            if not t.broken
                if t.isRes
                    resCount += 1
                else
                    supCount += 1

    string posTxt = posDir == 1 ? "LONG ACTIVE" : posDir == -1 ? "SHORT ACTIVE" : "flat"
    color  posCol = posDir == 1 ? colUp : posDir == -1 ? colDn : dim

    table.cell(dash, 0, 0, "TREND BREAKOUT ENTRIES", bgcolor = bgH, text_color = colRt, text_size = size.small)
    table.merge_cells(dash, 0, 0, 1, 0)

    table.cell(dash, 0, 1, "Nearest Res", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 1, na(resNow) ? "building" : str.tostring(resNow, format.mintick) + "   (" + str.tostring(resCount) + " lines)", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDn, text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(dash, 0, 2, "Nearest Sup", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 2, na(supNow) ? "building" : str.tostring(supNow, format.mintick) + "   (" + str.tostring(supCount) + " lines)", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colUp, text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(dash, 0, 3, "Distance To Res", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 3, na(distRes) ? "-" : str.tostring(distRes, "#.##") + " ATR", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(dash, 0, 4, "Distance To Sup", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 4, na(distSup) ? "-" : str.tostring(distSup, "#.##") + " ATR", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(dash, 0, 5, "Breakout Strength", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 5, "Up " + str.tostring(upScore, "#.0") + "  /  Dn " + str.tostring(dnScore, "#.0") + "   (need " + str.tostring(minStr, "#.#") + ")", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = math.max(upScore, dnScore) >= minStr ? colRt : dim, text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(dash, 0, 6, "Position", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 6, posTxt, bgcolor = bgR, text_color = posCol, text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(dash, 0, 7, "Last Risk", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colDashT, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 7, na(lastRisk) ? "-" : str.tostring(lastRisk, format.mintick) + "  (" + str.tostring(actMode == "Synthetic Estimate" or not hasReal ? "synth" : "real") + " vol)", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = dim, text_size = size.tiny)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  A L E R T S
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
alertcondition(buySig,  "TB - Buy Breakout",  "Trend Breakout Entries: strong bullish breakout above the resistance trendline on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")
alertcondition(sellSig, "TB - Sell Breakout", "Trend Breakout Entries: strong bearish breakout below the support trendline on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")
alertcondition(buyRetest,  "TB - Bullish Retest", "Trend Breakout Entries: price retested the broken resistance line from above on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")
alertcondition(sellRetest, "TB - Bearish Retest", "Trend Breakout Entries: price retested the broken support line from below on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")
alertcondition(buySig or sellSig, "TB - Any Breakout Signal", "Trend Breakout Entries: a breakout signal fired on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")

if buySig
    alert("Trend Breakout BUY - " + syminfo.ticker + " " + timeframe.period, alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if sellSig
    alert("Trend Breakout SELL - " + syminfo.ticker + " " + timeframe.period, alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  D A T A   W I N D O W   O U T P U T S
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
plot(resNow,  "Resistance Line", color = color.new(color.orange, 100), display = display.data_window)
plot(supNow,  "Support Line",    color = color.new(color.orange, 100), display = display.data_window)
plot(upScore, "Up Break Score",  color = color.new(color.orange, 100), display = display.data_window)
plot(dnScore, "Dn Break Score",  color = color.new(color.orange, 100), display = display.data_window)
plot(posDir,  "Position",        color = color.new(color.orange, 100), display = display.data_window)
